#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
I said this:

---

I think there's a bug in \encodeASCIIVariant or something like that.

I can set the Proto font to \ProtoCFont like this

\DeclareSourceProfile{Proto}
    {\EnglishProtoFont} 	{\color{ProtoColor}\mdseries}
    {\ProtoCFont} 		{\color{ProtoColor}\mdseries}

But this fails for all other letters X

\DeclareSourceProfile{Proto}
    {\EnglishProtoFont} 	{\color{ProtoColor}\mdseries}
    {\ProtoXFont} 		{\color{ProtoColor}\mdseries}

Any ideas what broke? This is from a recent commit of yours.

Also let me know the best way to toggle between Proto fonts on
a file by file basis with \renewcommand as needed.

---

You responded with this:

---

codex
Bug is here:

\newcommand{\EncodeASCIIVariant}[2]{%
  \directlua{tex.sprint(hebrew_to_ascii_variant(...))}%
}

`hebrew_to_ascii_variant` never becomes a Lua global. The recent commit introduced:

local function hebrew_to_ascii_variant(...)
...
function hebrew_to_ascii_variant(...)
...

Inside the same Lua chunk, that second definition hits the local name, not `_G`. So later `\directlua` calls see nil. Classic Lua footgun; Unix still innocent.

Fix either side:

\newcommand{\EncodeASCIIVariant}[2]{%
  \directlua{tex.sprint(paleotex.hebrew_to_ascii_variant("\luaescapestring{\detokenize{#2}}", "\luaescapestring{#1}"))}%
}

or rename the local implementation and export explicitly:

local function encode_ascii_variant(s, variant)
...
end

function paleotex.hebrew_to_ascii_variant(s, variant)
  return encode_ascii_variant(s, variant)
end

function hebrew_to_ascii_variant(s, variant)
  return paleotex.hebrew_to_ascii_variant(s, variant)
end

Best file-local toggle:

\begingroup
\renewcommand{\hProtoRenderer}{\ProtoCFont}
\include{1-genesis/49}
\endgroup

Or for another file:

\begingroup
\renewcommand{\hProtoRenderer}{\ProtoDFont}
\include{2-exodus/15}
\endgroup

Do not rerun `\DeclareSourceProfile{Proto}` for toggling; it uses `\newcommand`, so it is a declaration-time thing, not a knob.

---

Now, I want you to:
1. Fix the bug you mentioned above.
2. If possible, make it easier to toggle between whether \hPaleo (for example)
   means \hPaleoA, \hPaleoB, etc, on a file by file basis by using \renewcommand
   or \RenewDocumentCommand or however you have to do it.
EOF
